3.3 Computational cost
For a system with N atoms and at most Nc atoms inside Rc, the computational cost of Deep Potential is linear with N, similar to EAM, but requires a larger number of size independent operations. In all systems, Nc is size independent. Using Cu as an example,
both EAM and Deep Potential require OpNqNc operations to locate the atoms inside Rc.
Within EAM, 10NNc multiplications are needed to fit the potential. Within Deep Potential, 15NNc logNc operations are needed for the sorting, and 100NNc multiplications
